<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.6.4: Key Features of Linear Functions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00948</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.6.4: Key Features of Linear Functions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>971ea813-6f8d-43df-813a-d4b62713802f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001">      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Use the following information to answer questions 1 - 4.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">
        <quote id="quote-00001">The graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> is graphed below. Answer the questions about the linear function and its key features.</quote>
    </para>
      <para id="para-00003">
          <media alt="GRAPH OF A LINE WITH AN \(x\)-intercepts OF −3 AND \(y\)-intercepts OF 6.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_09_09_01.jpg" width="300"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">What is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00005">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00006">0</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">What key feature of the linear function is the point <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00008">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00009">The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept, or zero</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00010">What is the slope of the linear function?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00011">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00012">2</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00013">What part of the linear function is the point <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00014">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00015">The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts
  </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <para id="para-00016">Use the following information to answer questions 5 - 8.</para>
      <para id="para-00017">
        <quote id="quote-00002">The amount of money Adam saves in dollars is shown in the graph below.</quote>
    </para>
      
        <media alt="GRAPH THAT SHOWS THE TOTAL AMOUNT OF MONEY IN DOLLARS AS A FUNCTION OF NUMBER OF DAYS. THE FUNCTION IS A LINE WITH A POSITIVE SLOPE THAT PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS (0, 3) AND (1, 6).">
          <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_09_09_02.jpg"/>
        </media>
      
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00018">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the graph?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00019">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00020">The point is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.
  </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00006">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00021">What does the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts mean in the context of the problem</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00022">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary.</para>
          <para id="para-00023">When Adam started saving, he already had 3 dollars on
      day 0.
  </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00007">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00024">What is the slope?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00025">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00026">The slope is 3.
  </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00008">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00027">What does the slope mean in the context of the problem</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00028">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary.</para>
          <para id="para-00029">Every 1 day, Adam saves 3 dollars.
  </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <para id="para-00030">Use the following information to answer questions 9 - 12.</para>
      <para id="para-00031">
        <quote id="quote-00003">The graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>13</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> is graphed below. Identify the appropriate label for each key feature of the graph.</quote>
    </para>
      <para id="para-00032">
          <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_09_09_03.png"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <!--Q3a-->
      <exercise id="exer-00009">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00033">What is the key feature labeled <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> on the graph?
    </para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">

          <para id="para-00034">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00035"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, (0, 2), is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q3b-->
      <exercise id="exer-00010">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00036">What is the key feature labeled <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> on the graph?
    </para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">

          <para id="para-00037">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00038"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, (-6, 0), is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept or zero.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q3c-->
      <exercise id="exer-00011">
        <problem id="prob-00011">
          <para id="para-00039">What is the key feature labeled <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> on the graph?
    </para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00011">

          <para id="para-00040">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00041"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, (0, 0), is the origin.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q3d-->
      <exercise id="exer-00012">
        <problem id="prob-00012">
          <para id="para-00042">What is the key feature labeled <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> on the graph?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00012">

          <para id="para-00043">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00044"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>, is the slope.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
      <exercise>
        <problem>
        <para><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_4_6_4_SC"/></para>
        </problem>
        </exercise>
    </note>
    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>
      
    <section id="sect-00003">
      <title>Features of Linear Functions</title>
      <para id="para-00047">
          <media alt="">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_09_11_01.jpg" width="300"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <para id="para-00048">The graph of a linear function forms a line that goes on forever in both directions. Since the ends go to infinity and negative infinity, linear functions do not have maximums or minimums, unless their domain is restricted to a specific part of the graph.</para>
      <para id="para-00049">You can still pick out key features of linear functions.</para>
      <para id="para-00050">The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept, or zero, is where the line crosses the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis. This is where the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate is 0.</para>
      <para id="para-00051">In this linear function, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept, or zero, is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and written as the point <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00052">The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is where the line crosses the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis and the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate is 0.</para>
      <para id="para-00053">In this linear function, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and written as the point <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00054">The slope of the line can be found as in previous units as the change in <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> over the change in <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00055"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi mathvariant="normal">m</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mi mathvariant="normal">r</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">i</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">s</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">e</m:mi></m:mrow></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mi mathvariant="normal">r</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">u</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mi mathvariant="normal">c</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">h</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">a</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">n</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">g</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">e</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mrow><m:mi mathvariant="normal">i</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">n</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi mathvariant="normal">y</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mi mathvariant="normal">c</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">h</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">a</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">n</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">g</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">e</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mrow><m:mi mathvariant="normal">i</m:mi><m:mi mathvariant="normal">n</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi mathvariant="normal">x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00056">The slope of this linear function is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <note class="try" id="note-00002">
  <title>Try It: Features of Linear Functions</title>
      <para id="para-00057">Find the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the linear function graphed below. Write each answer as a point.</para>
      <para id="para-00058">
          <media alt="">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_09_11_02.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      
        <exercise id="exer-00013">
          <problem id="prob-00013">
            <para id="para-00059">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.
  </para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00013">
            <para id="para-00060">Here is how to find the intercepts of a linear function:</para>
            <para id="para-00061">Since the line crosses the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis at about <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2.75</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, that is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept.</para>
            <para id="para-00062">Since the line crosses the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, that is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </note>
    </section>
    </section>
    
  </content>
